cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below and also credit the original sources listed in docs/SOURCES.md."
type: dataset
title: "AyurKB: a bilingual, hybrid Ayurveda knowledge base for expert systems"
abstract: >-
  AyurKB links Ayurvedic diagnosis, materia medica, remedies and modern scientific evidence in one relational
  dataset, in English and Hindi, with every Sanskrit term in IAST and Devanagari. It is built only from
  authoritative or openly licensed sources (Ministry of Ayush NAMASTE, WHO, USDA, GBIF, Wikidata, NLM,
  PubChem, Europe PMC and a DOI-registered CC BY herb database), cross-validated, checked against 565
  published case reports and benchmarked with machine-learning experiments E1-E8.
authors:
